# Developer Architectural Analysis: Heatwave Prediction System

This document provides a deep, code-level structural breakdown of the Heatwave Prediction project. It is intended for software engineers and data scientists looking to understand, maintain, or extend the existing Haskell + Vanilla JS stack.

---

## 1. Project Structure

The project strictly divides raw UI static files and a Haskell backend serving cross-origin APIs.

```
heatwave-project/
├── backend/
│   ├── heatwave-backend/
│   │   ├── app/
│   │   │   └── Main.hs         # Core server instance, routing, startup routines
│   │   ├── src/
│   │   │   ├── Types.hs        # Data Models and JSON encoding/decoding instances
│   │   │   ├── Database.hs     # SQLite persistence layer and schema definitions
│   │   │   ├── DataLoader.hs   # CSV parsing and feature vector extraction map
│   │   │   └── ML.hs           # Pure functional Logistic Regression implementation
│   │   ├── data.csv            # Static ML training dataset
│   │   └── heatwave-backend.cabal # Cabal package spec
└── frontend/
    ├── index.html              # Main application markup layout
    ├── styles.css              # Custom layout, styling, animations (CSS)
    └── app.js                  # DOM Manipulation, Fetch logic, and Chart.js integration
```

---

## 2. File-by-File Analysis

### Backend

#### [app/Main.hs](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/app/Main.hs)
- **Purpose**: The entry point for the REST API. Handles HTTP logic, manages state (ML model weights), and trains the initial model.
- **Functions**:
  - `main :: IO ()` - App bootstrapper. Initializes SQLite DB, extracts data from [data.csv](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/data.csv), trains the Logistic Regression model, saves weights in an `IORef`, and bootstraps the Scotty server with CORS enabled. Outlines GET `/health`, POST `/predict`, GET `/history`.
- **Inputs/Outputs**: No formal params. Returns `IO ()`.
- **Variables**: `initialWeights`, `learningRate = 0.001`, `epochs = 5000`, `weightsRef`.
- **Imports**: `Web.Scotty`, `Network.Wai.Middleware.Cors`, `Data.Aeson`, `Control.Monad.IO.Class`, `Types`, `Database`, `DataLoader`, `ML`, `Data.IORef`.
- **Dependents**: Serves the frontend directly. Relies on all other [.hs](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/src/ML.hs) modules.

#### [src/Types.hs](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/src/Types.hs)
- **Purpose**: The domain model. Connects JSON and SQLite payloads into typed Haskell records.
- **Classes/Types**:
  - `HeatwaveData` - Training struct. `date, region, maxTemp, minTemp, humidity, heatwave`.
  - `PredictRequest` - Input struct. `reqMaxTemp, reqMinTemp, reqHumidity, reqDate, reqRegion`.
  - `PredictResponse` - Output struct. `probability, prediction`.
  - `HistoryRecord` - Database struct. `hId, hDate...`
- **Instances**: Derived `FromJSON/ToJSON` via `Generic`. Custom `FromRow/ToRow` for SQLite row bindings.
- **Imports**: `Data.Aeson`, `GHC.Generics`, `Database.SQLite.Simple`, `Data.Text`.
- **Dependents**: Imported by EVERY module in the backend.

#### [src/ML.hs](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/src/ML.hs)
- **Purpose**: A pure, dependency-free mathematical module running Binary Logistic Regression.
- **Functions**:
  - `sigmoid :: Double -> Double` - Squeezes numbers between 0 and 1.
  - `dotProduct :: [Double] -> [Double] -> Double` - Computes the vector dot product $\sum (w_i * x_i)$.
  - `predictProb :: [Double] -> [Double] -> Double` - Maps weights * features through `sigmoid`.
  - `predictClass :: [Double] -> [Double] -> Double -> Int` - Casts probability logic strictly > than threshold (`0.5`).
  - `updateWeights :: [Double] -> Double -> [([Double], Double)] -> [Double]` - Runs one full pass (epoch) of gradient descent computing gradient [(actual - prediction) * x](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/frontend/app.js#3-14). 
  - `train :: Int -> Double -> [([Double], Double)] -> [Double] -> [Double]` - Recursively calls `updateWeights` for $N$ epochs.
- **Imports**: [Types.hs](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/src/Types.hs)
- **Dependents**: [Main.hs](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/app/Main.hs)

#### [src/DataLoader.hs](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/src/DataLoader.hs)
- **Purpose**: Responsible for consuming raw data streams and structuring feature matrices for the AI.
- **Functions**:
  - `parseNamedRecord` instance - Cassava's hook for mapping CSV columns to `HeatwaveData`.
  - `loadData :: FilePath -> IO [HeatwaveData]` - Performs Lazy IO read on CSV and runs structural decoding.
  - `extractFeatures :: [HeatwaveData] -> [([Double], Double)]` - Converts records to structured vectors: [([Bias (1.0), MaxTemp, MinTemp, Humidity], TargetLabel)](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/frontend/app.js#3-14).
- **Imports**: `Data.ByteString.Lazy`, `Data.Csv`, `Data.Vector`, `Types`.
- **Dependents**: [Main.hs](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/app/Main.hs)

#### [src/Database.hs](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/src/Database.hs)
- **Purpose**: Wraps SQLite bindings into neat side-effect IO calls.
- **Functions**:
  - `dbName :: String` - Static variable `"heatwave.db"`.
  - `initDB :: IO ()` - Ensures the table `history` is mapped correctly using raw SQL `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`.
  - `savePrediction :: PredictRequest -> PredictResponse -> IO ()` - Appends `INSERT` statements using parameterized queries [(?, ?, ?, ...)](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/frontend/app.js#3-14).
  - `getHistory :: IO [HistoryRecord]` - Queries the table with a strict bounds check (`LIMIT 50`) ordered by desc.
- **Imports**: `Database.SQLite.Simple`, `Types`, `Data.Text`
- **Dependents**: [Main.hs](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/backend/heatwave-backend/app/Main.hs)

### Frontend

#### [app.js](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/frontend/app.js)
- **Purpose**: Controls interaction, manages state view overlays, and pushes requests entirely client-side.
- **Functions**:
  - [switchTab(tabId, element)](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/frontend/app.js#3-14) - Toggles CSS `active` classes for SPA emulation dynamically.
  - Event Listener (`submit`) - Prevents page reload, parses HTML inputs (`reqDate`, `reqMaxTemp`, etc.), formats JSON string, and calls `fetch()`. Wait state is shown until JSON received, then pushes into [showResults()](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/frontend/app.js#45-63).
  - [showResults(data)](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/frontend/app.js#45-63) - Mutates the UI elements (circular `.style.background` property based on probability array) for aesthetic outcome.
  - [loadHistory()](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/frontend/app.js#66-77) - Fires asynchronous `fetch()` to `/history`, piping data arrays into table render and graph render.
  - [renderTable(data)](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/frontend/app.js#78-99) - Procedurally generates DOM nodes `<tr><td>...</td></tr>` for table logic logic.
  - [renderChart(data)](file:///e:/antigravity%20haskell%20-%20Copy/frontend/app.js#100-148) - Destroys the pre-existing `historyChart` cache on `Canvas`, mutates payloads into arrays (Reverse map to fix ordering), and bootstraps a multi-axis `Chart.js` graph.

