## 8. Critical Code Snippets Explained

### ML Prediction Engine (Pure math logic inside Haskell)
```haskell
-- Maps values to Sigmoid Probability mathematically
predictProb :: [Double] -> [Double] -> Double
predictProb weights features = 1.0 / (1.0 + exp (-(sum $ zipWith (*) weights features)))
```

### Database Persistence Engine
```haskell
savePrediction :: PredictRequest -> PredictResponse -> IO ()
savePrediction req res = do
    conn <- open dbName
    -- Pure parameterization blocks malicious SQL Injections inherently
    execute conn "INSERT INTO history (date, region, max_temp, min_temp, humidity, probability, prediction) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)"
        (reqDate req, reqRegion req, reqMaxTemp req, reqMinTemp req, reqHumidity req, probability res, prediction res)
    close conn
```

### Frontend State Controller
```javascript
// Destructures JSON prediction mapping styles logically onto the View Canvas
function showResults(data) {
    const isHeatwave = data.prediction === 1;
    const probPct = (data.probability * 100).toFixed(1);
    
    // Updates UI string state based on ML output
    document.getElementById('res-status').innerText = isHeatwave ? "Heatwave Expected 🔥" : "No Heatwave 🌤️";
    
    // Updates UI logic gradient circle map for data visibility
    const color = isHeatwave ? "#e84118" : "#44bd32";
    document.getElementById('prob-circle').style.background = `conic-gradient(${color} ${probPct}%, #eee 0%)`;
}
```

